# Source: https://github.com/samtools/htslib/issues/1085
# Symptom: BED6 file (or bedGraph-like) where col 4 (name) contains only
#   integers and col 6 contains strand symbols; htslib auto-detection misreads
#   exactly 5 or 6 columns with an integer col 4 as a FASTQ index (.fqi)
#   instead of BED, causing tabix to fail with "FASTQ-IDX BGZF-compressed
#   index data" and "Exec format error".  The fix is to use a non-integer or
#   real-valued col 4 (e.g. 100.0 rather than 100).
# Format: chrom start end name(integer) score strand
chr21	1000	2000	100	0	+
chr21	3000	4000	200	0	-
chr22	5000	6000	150	0	+
chr22	7000	8000	75	0	-
